    "## 4. Tokenization and cleaning\n",
    "A neural network can't read text, only numbers. Step one is splitting a sentence into **tokens** (words and punctuation).\n",
    "\n",
    "- Lowercase everything (so \"The\" and \"the\" are one word).\n",
    "- Put spaces around punctuation so `\"hello,\"` becomes `hello` `,`. This includes French quotes `« »`.\n",
    "- French glues small words with apostrophes (`l'homme`, `j'ai`, `qu'il`). We split these as `l'` `homme` so the model learns `l'` once instead of memorising every glued variant.\n",
    "- Then split on whitespace (this also handles French non-breaking spaces before `?` and `!`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "5f34c111",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[\"l'\", 'homme', 'a', 'dit', ':', '«', 'je', \"n'\", 'ai', 'pas', 'faim', '!', '»']\n",
      "[\"don't\", 'worry', ',', \"it's\", 'fine', '.']\n",
      "Pairs after length filter + cap: 60000\n",
      "(['what', 'would', 'be', 'your', 'reason', '?'], ['quelle', 'serait', 'votre', 'raison', '?'])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "PUNCT = re.compile(r\"([.,!?;:\\\"()\\[\\]«»…])\")\n",
    "ELISION = re.compile(r\"\\b(l|d|j|n|s|c|m|t|qu|jusqu|lorsqu|puisqu)['’]\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def tokenize(s):\n",
    "    s = s.lower().strip()\n",
    "    s = ELISION.sub(r\"\\1' \", s)       # l'homme -> l' homme\n",
    "    s = PUNCT.sub(r\" \\1 \", s)\n",
    "    return s.split()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(tokenize(\"L'homme a dit : « Je n'ai pas faim ! »\"))\n",
    "print(tokenize(\"Don't worry, it's fine.\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "pairs = []\n",
    "for en, fr in raw_pairs:\n",
    "    src, trg = tokenize(en), tokenize(fr)\n",
    "    if 1 <= len(src) <= MAX_LEN and 1 <= len(trg) <= MAX_LEN:\n",
    "        pairs.append((src, trg))\n",
    "\n",
    "random.shuffle(pairs)\n",
    "pairs = pairs[:MAX_PAIRS]\n",
    "print(\"Pairs after length filter + cap:\", len(pairs))\n",
    "print(pairs[0])"
   ]
  },
